# KingOfFate -- line ending policy
#
# The project is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true locally), so git
# rewrites text files to CRLF in the working tree by default. Two kinds of file
# must not be rewritten:
#
#   * the test fixtures under tests/fixtures/assets/ -- make_fixtures.py --check
#     and verify_decoders.py compare them BYTE FOR BYTE with what the generator
#     produces, so a line ending change is a test failure on a fresh checkout;
#   * anything already treated as binary (SFF/SND containers contain NUL bytes,
#     so git classifies them as binary on its own).
#
# Everything else keeps the default behaviour: LF in the repository, CRLF in the
# working tree on Windows. The .air parser handles both (it splits on \n and
# strips \r), so character files are safe either way.

tests/fixtures/assets/**  -text
